7	// BUILD-ONLY extension of the build path (the R2.3 deliverable (2)): this is a
8	// SECOND compiled TU for the SAME (decoder × adamw) cell, selected by the GEMM
9	// impl token. It is NOT wired into compile.py / dispatch — the parity gate
10	// (tests/hw/test_decoder_tc.py PART 2) JIT-loads it via cpp_extension.load and
11	// drives it directly through the pybind entry below (mirroring the scalar
12	// dispatch.cpp:630-651 launch). No setup.py glob change, no dispatch routing.
13	//
14	// The pybind entry `tc_train_step` runs ONE Fork-B TC step over a flat fp32
15	// param blob in place, returning (mean loss, reduced weight grad [total]) so the
16	// gate can compare every grad per-tensor vs the bf16-rounded fp64 oracle (the
17	// keystone validation — the CPU mirror does NOT cover tile-batched P1).
18	//
19	// HONESTY: this exercises the REAL tensor-core path (HGMMA in SASS, verified by
20	// the SASS audit in test_decoder_tc.py). No scalar fallback, no surrogate.
21	
